# dtd: adapt the photometric warping loss for stereo, batch-size-agnostically.
#
# base: 9d965a626c513727c73311fadd796b83c931462f
# upstream: https://github.com/madhubabuv/dtd
#
# Used by utils/image_warping_loss.py. Unlike the other patches in this directory
# this one changes behavior, so each piece is spelled out:
#
#   losses/photometric_loss.py  add __call__, so PhotometricLoss can be invoked
#                               directly the way image_warping_loss.py uses it.
#   models/image_warping.py     forward(..., intrinsics_target=None): stereo warping
#                               projects into the *other* camera, which may not share
#                               intrinsics with the source.
#   models/image_warping.py     padding_mode "border" -> "zeros". THIS CHANGES LOSS
#                               VALUES. Border padding replicates edge pixels, which
#                               fabricates plausible photometric matches outside the
#                               frustum; zeros does not, so out-of-view pixels are
#                               penalized instead of rewarded.
#   models/utils.py             drop batch_size from BackprojectDepth/Project3D and
#                               build the coordinate grids per-forward. Upstream bakes
#                               a fixed batch size into nn.Parameters at construction,
#                               which breaks on the last (short) batch of an epoch.
#                               Also register_buffer instead of nn.Parameter, so the
#                               grids follow .to(device) and stay out of the optimizer.
